  "question": {
    "text": "Let the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math> be rotated by an&nbsp;angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;about its line of intersection with the plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is the distance of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math> from the new position of the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
